.\" The manual page of the Linux packages (NP-055).
.TH KOONAPIN-HOST 1 "October 2026" "Koona Pin" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
koonapin-host \- native messaging host of Koona Pin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B koonapin-host
.I origin-or-manifest
.RI [ extension-id ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The browser starts
.B koonapin-host
for each message of the Koona Pin extension; it is not run by hand. It passes the message to
.BR koonapin (1)
over a socket in
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/koonapin
and returns the answer. A saved link starts a closed app hidden.
.PP
The browsers find it through the manifests
.I app.koona.pin.json
the package puts in
.IR /etc/opt/chrome ,
.IR /etc/opt/edge ,
.I /etc/chromium
and
.I /usr/lib/mozilla
(native-messaging-hosts).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR koonapin (1)
